        {
          "fields": {
            "ParentID": "@parent:ID",
            "Name": "Statistics Pass",
            "CategoryID": "@lookup:MJ: AI Agent Categories.Name=Research and Analysis",
            "Description": "Code-based agent (no LLM) that MEASURES the data before any architecture is chosen. Assembles the training partition through the same FeatureAssembly executor training uses, carves the locked holdout away and describes ONLY what remains (describing the holdout would stop MLModel.HoldoutMetrics being an honest number), and calls the sidecar's read-only /describe for class balance, per-feature association with the target, cardinality, missingness and correlations. Derives the feature hints (leakage-dominance, near-duplicate-of-target, id-like, constant, high-cardinality, high-missingness, collinear) and evaluates each proposed candidate against the StatisticalGate rows its ML Component Type INHERITS. Writes Statistics + GateReports onto the plan. The orchestrator forces this sub-agent once the plan is describable, exactly once — re-measuring the same rows cannot change the answer.",
            "TypeID": "@lookup:MJ: AI Agent Types.Name=Loop",
            "Status": "Active",
            "ExecutionOrder": 3,
            "ExposeAsAction": false,
            "InvocationMode": "Sub-Agent",
            "DriverClass": "PredictiveStudioStatisticsPassAgent",
            "IconClass": "fa-solid fa-ruler-combined",
            "PayloadDownstreamPaths": [
              "*"
            ],
            "PayloadUpstreamPaths": [
              "Statistics",
              "Statistics.*",
              "GateReports",
              "GateReports.*"
            ]
          },
          "primaryKey": {
            "ID": "BC813639-C732-4D43-827E-C2AF42FBF457"
          }
        },
        {
          "fields": {
            "ParentID": "@parent:ID",
            "Name": "Architect",
            "CategoryID": "@lookup:MJ: AI Agent Categories.Name=Research and Analysis",
            "Description": "Makes the architecture decision — what KIND of model this should be — from the measured evidence the Statistics Pass produced rather than from the goal statement. Chooses one of four shapes: commit (one family, when the evidence is clear), defer (race several, when it is not), reify (name the generalized parent the candidates are variations of), or compose (build a custom model by filling a structure's slots). Never proposes a candidate whose gate report says Admissible: false, and records every candidate considered with its rationale so the rejections are auditable too. A composed graph is validated against the real component tree — slots, accepted types, arity, no abstract instantiation — before anything runs.",
            "TypeID": "@lookup:MJ: AI Agent Types.Name=Loop",
            "Status": "Active",
            "ExecutionOrder": 4,
            "ExposeAsAction": false,
            "InvocationMode": "Sub-Agent",
            "IconClass": "fa-solid fa-sitemap",
            "PayloadDownstreamPaths": [
              "*"
            ],
            "PayloadUpstreamPaths": [
